          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            One of the types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetime"} pp-
            = succeed "-solution" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitational+wave"} gravitational wave
            %em M-wave
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hull84"}> Hull 1984
            ). Survey includes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Philip05"} Philip 2005 p. 94
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bandos12"} Bandos 12
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            the M-wave becomes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-brane
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            (
            %a{:href => "#BergshoeffTwonsend96"}> Bergshoeff &amp; Townsend 1996
            ).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of M-waves and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            are argued to correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+string"} self-dual string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
            solutions in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            theory of the M5 (
            %a{:href => "#ChuIsono13"}> Chu &amp; Isono 2012
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#spin_structure Spin structure
          %p
            That the spinor-to-vector pairing on the M-wave takes values in just one of the two light rays is made fully explicit in
            %a{:href => "#Philip05"} Philip 05, p. 94
          %p
            This is the pairing of chiral spinors in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 1 + 1
          %h3#relation_to_m2branes_at_adesingularities Relation to M2-Branes at ADE-Singularities
          %p
            The M-wave may
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersection"} intersect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
            (show in
            %a{:href => "#BPST09"} BPST 09, bottom of p. 13
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            for the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} ABJM model
